H6000.definition:
the same as H5999 (עָמָל);
Amal, an Israelite
KJV: Amal.

H6001.definition:
from H5998 (עָמַל);
toiling; concretely, a laborer; figuratively, sorrowful
KJV: that laboureth, that is a misery, had taken (labour), wicked, workman.

H6002.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
Amalek, a descendant of Esau; also his posterity and their country
KJV: Amalek.

H6003.definition:
patronymically from H6002 (עֲמָלֵק);
an Amalekite (or collectively the Amalekites) or descendants of Amalek
KJV: Amalekite(-s).

H6004.definition:
a primitive root;
to associate; by implication, to overshadow (by huddling together)
KJV: become dim, hide.

H6005.definition:
from H5973 (עִם) and with a pronominal suffix inserted; with us (is) God;
Immanuel, a type name of Isaiah's son
KJV: Immanuel.

H6006.definition:
or עָמַשׂ; a primitive root;
to load, i.e. impose aburden (or figuratively, infliction)
KJV: be borne, (heavy) burden (self), lade, load, put.

H6007.definition:
from H6006 (עָמַס) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has loaded;
Amasjah, an Israelite
KJV: Amasiah.

H6008.definition:
from H5971 (עַם) and H5703 (עַד); people of time;
Amad, a place in Palestine
KJV: Amad.

H6009.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causatively, make) deep (literally or figuratively)
KJV: (be, have, make, seek) deep(-ly), depth, be profound.

H6010.definition:
from H6009 (עָמַק);
a vale (i.e. broad depression)
KJV: dale, vale, valley (often used as a part of proper names). See also H1025 (בֵּית הָעֵמֶק).

H6012.definition:
from H6009 (עָמַק);
deep (literally or figuratively)
KJV: deeper, depth, strange.

H6013.definition:
from H6009 (עָמַק);
deep (literally or figuratively)
KJV: ([idiom] exceeding) deep (thing).

H6015.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6785 (צֶמֶר);
wool
KJV: wool.

H6016.definition:
from H6014 (עָמַר);
properly, a heap, i.e. a sheaf; also an omer, as a dry measure
KJV: omer, sheaf.

H6017.definition:
from H6014 (עָמַר); a (ruined) heap;
Amorah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gomorrah.

H6018.definition:
from H6014 (עָמַר); heaping;
Omri, an Israelite
KJV: Omri.

H6019.definition:
probably from H5971 (עַם) and H7311 (רוּם); high people;
Amram, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Amram.

H6020.definition:
from H6019 (עַמְרָם);
an Amramite or descendant of Amram
KJV: Amramite.

H6021.definition:
from H6006 (עָמַס); burden;
Amasa, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Amasa.

H6022.definition:
from H6006 (עָמַס); burdensome;
Amasai, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Amasai.

H6023.definition:
probably from H6006 (עָמַס); burdensome;
Amashsay, an Israelite
KJV: Amashai.

H6024.definition:
from the same as H6025 (עֵנָב); fruit;
Anab, a place in Palestine
KJV: Anab.

H6025.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to bear fruit;
a grape
KJV: (ripe) grape, wine.

H6026.definition:
a primitive root;
to be soft or pliable, i.e. (figuratively) effeminate or luxurious
KJV: delicate(-ness), (have) delight (self), sport self.

H6027.definition:
from H6026 (עָנַג);
luxury
KJV: delight, pleasant.

H6029.definition:
a primitive root;
to lace fast
KJV: bind, tie.

H6030.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to eye or (generally) to heed, i.e. pay attention; by implication, to respond; by extension to begin to speak; specifically to sing, shout, testify, announce
KJV: give account, afflict (by mistake for H6031 (עָנָה)), (cause to, give) answer, bring low (by mistake for H6031 (עָנָה)), cry, hear, Leannoth, lift up, say, [idiom] scholar, (give a) shout, sing (together by course), speak, testify, utter, (bear) witness. See also H1042 (בֵּית עֲנוֹת), H1043 (בֵּית עֲנָת).

H6031.definition:
a primitive root (possibly rather identical with H6030 (עָנָה) through the idea of looking down or browbeating);
to depress literally or figuratively, transitive or intransitive (in various applications, as follows)
KJV: abase self, afflict(-ion, self), answer (by mistake for H6030 (עָנָה)), chasten self, deal hardly with, defile, exercise, force, gentleness, humble (self), hurt, ravish, sing (by mistake for H6030 (עָנָה)), speak (by mistake for H6030 (עָנָה)), submit self, weaken, [idiom] in any wise.

H6032.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6030 (עָנָה)
{properly, to eye or (generally) to heed, i.e. pay attention; by implication, to respond; by extension to begin to speak; specifically to sing, shout, testify, announce}
KJV: answer, speak.

H6033.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6031 (עָנָה)
{to depress literally or figuratively, transitive or intransitive (in various applications, as follows)}
KJV: poor.

H6034.definition:
probably from H6030 (עָנָה); an answer;
Anah, the name of two Edomites and one Edomitess
KJV: Anah.

H6035.definition:
or (by intermixture with H6041 (עָנִי)) עָנָיו; from H6031 (עָנָה);
depressed (figuratively), in mind (gentle) or circumstances (needy, especially saintly)
KJV: humble, lowly, meek, poor. Compare H6041 (עָנִי).

H6036.definition:
passive participle from the same as H6025 (עֵנָב); borne (as fruit);
Anub, an Israelite
KJV: Anub.

H6037.definition:
feminine of H6035 (עָנָו);
mildness (royal); also (concretely) oppressed
KJV: gentleness, meekness.

H6038.definition:
from H6035 (עָנָו);
condescension, human and subjective (modesty), or divine and objective (clemency)
KJV: gentleness, humility, meekness.

H6040.definition:
from H6031 (עָנָה);
depression, i.e. misery
KJV: afflicted(-ion), trouble.

H6041.definition:
from H6031 (עָנָה); (practically the same as H6035 (עָנָו), although the margin constantly disputes this, making H6035 (עָנָו) subjective and objective);
depressed, in mind or circumstances
KJV: afflicted, humble, lowly, needy, poor.

H6042.definition:
from H6031 (עָנָה); afflicted;
Unni, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Unni.

H6043.definition:
from H6030 (עָנָה); Jah has answered;
Anajah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Anaiah.

H6044.definition:
for plural of H5869 (עַיִן); fountains;
Anim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Anim.

H6045.definition:
from H6031 (עָנָה);
ado, i.e. (generally) employment or (specifically) an affair
KJV: business, travail.

H6046.definition:
from the dual of H5869 (עַיִן); two fountains;
Anem, a place in Palestine
KJV: Anem.

H6047.definition:
as if plural of some Egyptian word;
Anamim, a son of Mizraim and his descendants, with their country
KJV: Anamim.

H6048.definition:
of foreign origin;
Anammelek, an Assyrian deity
KJV: Anammelech.

H6049.definition:
a primitive root; to cover; used only as a denominative from H6051 (עָנָן), to cloud over;
figuratively, to act covertly, i.e. practise magic
KJV: [idiom] bring, enchanter, Meonemin, observe(-r of) times, soothsayer, sorcerer.

H6050.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6051 (עָנָן)
{a cloud (as covering the sky), i.e. the nimbus or thunder-cloud}
KJV: cloud.

H6051.definition:
from H6049 (עָנַן);
a cloud (as covering the sky), i.e. the nimbus or thunder-cloud
KJV: cloud(-y).

H6052.definition:
the same as H6051 (עָנָן); cloud;
Anan, an Israelite
KJV: Anan.

H6053.definition:
feminine of H6051 (עָנָן);
cloudiness
KJV: cloud.

H6054.definition:
from H6051 (עָנָן); cloudy;
Anani, an Israelite
KJV: Anani.

H6055.definition:
from H6049 (עָנַן) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has covered;
Ananjah, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Ananiah.

H6056.definition:
(Aramaic) or עֶנֶף; (Aramaic), corresponding to H6057 (עָנָף)
{a twig (as covering the limbs)}
KJV: bough, branch.

H6057.definition:
from an unused root meaning to cover;
a twig (as covering the limbs)
KJV: bough, branch.

H6058.definition:
from the same as H6057 (עָנָף);
branching
KJV: full of branches.

H6060.definition:
from H6059 (עָנַק);
a necklace (as if strangling)
KJV: chain.

H6061.definition:
the same as H6060 (עָנָק);
Anak, a Canaanite
KJV: Anak.

H6062.definition:
patronymically from H6061 (עָנָק);
an Anakite or descendant of Anak
KJV: Anakim.

H6063.definition:
probably for H5288 (נַעַר);
Aner, a Amorite, also a place in Palestine
KJV: Aner.

H6064.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to urge; by implication, to inflict apenalty, specifically, to fine
KJV: amerce, condemn, punish, [idiom] surely.

H6065.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6066 (עֹנֶשׁ);
a mulct
KJV: confiscation.

H6066.definition:
from H6064 (עָנַשׁ);
a fine
KJV: punishment, tribute.

H6067.definition:
from H6030 (עָנָה); answer;
Anath, an Israelite
KJV: Anath.

H6068.definition:
plural of H6067 (עֲנָת);
Anathoth, the name of two Israelites, also of a place in Pal
KJV: Anathoth.

H6069.definition:
or עַנְּתוֹתִי; patrial from H6068 (עֲנָתוֹת);
a Antothite or inhabitant of Anathoth
KJV: of Anathoth, Anethothite, Anetothite, Antothite.

H6070.definition:
from the same as H6068 (עֲנָתוֹת) and H3050 (יָהּ); answers of Jah;
Anthothijah, an Israelite
KJV: Antothijah.

H6071.definition:
from H6072 (עָסַס);
must or fresh grape-juice (as just trodden out)
KJV: juice, new (sweet) wine.

H6072.definition:
a primitive root;
to squeeze out juice; figuratively, to trample
KJV: tread down.

H6073.definition:
from an unused root meaning to cover;
a bough (as covering the tree)
KJV: branch.

H6074.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6073 (עֳפֶא);
a twig; bough, i.e. (collectively) foliage
KJV: leaves.

H6075.definition:
a primitive root;
to swell; figuratively, be elated
KJV: be lifted up, presume.

H6076.definition:
from H6075 (עָפַל);
a tumor; also a mound, i.e. fortress
KJV: emerod, fort, strong hold, tower.

H6077.definition:
the same as H6076 (עֹפֶל);
Ophel, a ridge in Jerusalem
KJV: Ophel.

H6078.definition:
from an unused noun (denoting a place in Palestine; from an unused root of uncertain meaning);
an Ophnite (collectively) or inhabitants of Ophen
KJV: Ophni.

H6079.definition:
from H5774 (עוּף);
an eyelash (as fluttering); figuratively, morning ray
KJV: dawning, eye-lid.

H6081.definition:
probably a variation of H6082 (עֹפֶר); gazelle;
Epher, the name of an Arabian and of two Israelites
KJV: Epher.

H6082.definition:
from H6080 (עָפַר);
a fawn (from the dusty color)
KJV: young roe (hart).

H6083.definition:
from H6080 (עָפַר);
dust (as powdered or gray); hence, clay, earth, mud
KJV: ashes, dust, earth, ground, morter, powder, rubbish.

H6084.definition:
feminine of H6082 (עֹפֶר); female fawn;
Ophrah, the name of an Israelite and of two places in Palestine
KJV: Ophrah.

H6085.definition:
from the same as H6081 (עֵפֶר); fawn-like;
Ephron, the name of a Canaanite and of two places in Palestine
KJV: Ephron, Ephrain (from the margin).

H6086.definition:
from H6095 (עָצָה);
a tree (from its firmness); hence, wood (plural sticks)
KJV: [phrase] carpenter, gallows, helve, [phrase] pine, plank, staff, stalk, stick, stock, timber, tree, wood.

H6087.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to carve, i.e. fabricate or fashion; hence (in a bad sense) to worry, pain or anger
KJV: displease, grieve, hurt, make, be sorry, vex, worship, wrest.

H6088.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6087 (עָצַב);
to afflict
KJV: lamentable.

H6089.definition:
from H6087 (עָצַב);
an earthen vessel; usually (painful) toil; also a pang (whether of body or mind)
KJV: grievous, idol, labor, sorrow.

H6090.definition:
a variation of H6089 (עֶצֶב);
an idol (as fashioned); also pain (bodily or mental)
KJV: idol, sorrow, [idiom] wicked.

H6091.definition:
from H6087 (עָצַב);
an (idolatrous) image
KJV: idol, image.

H6092.definition:
from H6087 (עָצַב);
a (hired) workman
KJV: labour.

H6093.definition:
from H6087 (עָצַב);
worrisomeness, i.e. labor or pain
KJV: sorrow, toil.

H6094.definition:
from H6087 (עָצַב);
a idol; also, a pain or wound
KJV: sorrow, wound.

H6095.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to fasten (or make firm), i.e. to close (the eyes)
KJV: shut.

H6096.definition:
from H6095 (עָצָה);
the spine (as giving firmness to the body)
KJV: backbone.

H6097.definition:
feminine of H6086 (עֵץ);
timber
KJV: trees.

H6098.definition:
from H3289 (יָעַץ);
advice; by implication, plan; also prudence
KJV: advice, advisement, counsel(l-(or)), purpose.

H6099.definition:
or עָצֻם; passive participle of H6105 (עָצַם);
powerful (specifically, a paw); by implication, numerous
KJV: [phrase] feeble, great, mighty, must, strong.
